  "adaptations": [
    "Protocol v6 adds fixed explicit little-endian setup98/report104/ack106-byte messages, each bounded to256bytes.",
    "Server receives at most one coalesced report per player/tick, checks world/player/object/full force identities and monotonically increasing sequence.",
    "A report tick uses the original collision-checked destination without another integration; intervening ticks advance velocity with two swept substeps, no CMoveMgr commands/gravity/acceleration integration.",
    "Source animation/clearance retains controls each60Hz tick. Neutralize expired controls and hold velocity after30ticks without a report; explicit bounded extrapolation policy.",
    "Network force generation observes both original player movement_revision and engine pose_revision, without mutating solo force codes or gameplay teleport paths.",
    "ACK motion is captured at report acceptance, not from later extrapolated poses; wire client correction and complete private event/audio/effect delivery remain subsequent work."
  ]
